<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Hardened-runtime exceptions for the autodeck app process (Contents/MacOS/autodeck).
     Keep this list minimal; every entry weakens the runtime's protection.

     allow-unsigned-executable-memory: numba (librosa's onset/beat helpers) compiles functions
       with LLVM at runtime and maps that machine code executable without MAP_JIT (llvmlite's
       own memory manager), and reloads compiled functions from NUMBA_CACHE_DIR the same way.
       Under the hardened runtime that mapping is refused without this entitlement and librosa
       crashes on first use. (allow-jit alone is not enough: it only covers MAP_JIT memory.)

     Deliberately NOT here:
       disable-library-validation: every dylib/.so in the bundle is signed with our own
         Developer ID, so library validation passes; the self-updated yt-dlp is pure Python.
       allow-jit: nothing in this process allocates MAP_JIT memory (torch/onnxruntime/
         ctranslate2 run precompiled kernels; WebKit's JS JIT runs in its own XPC process). -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key><true/>
</dict>
</plist>
